 resources and rotate the squad throughout the remainder of the second half. Clinical Management to the Final Whistle The final half-hour was characterized by a series of tactical substitutions from both managers. Players like Simion Michez , Anas Tajaouart , and Leandro Rousseau were introduced to see out the result. While the scoring pace slowed, the competitive edge remained, evidenced by a yellow card for Adeshina Ayodele in the 84th minute. When the final whistle blew after four minutes of stoppage time, the scoreboard reflected a night of total dominance for RAAL La Louvière . Their clinical finishing and ability to score at pivotal moments proved too much for Lommel United to handle, securing a memorable victory in front of their home supporters."
