      "description": "Watch KV Mechelen vs Standard Liege highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 17, 2026. Fans in the Jupiler Pro League witnessed a game of extraordinary shifts and late drama as KV Mechelen hosted Lommel United on August 17, 2026. The atmosphere was electric for a clash that promised intensity from the opening whistle to the very final seconds. Early Shocks for the Hosts Lommel United started the match with intent, catching the hosts off guard early on. In the 9th minute, Bernard Nguene found the back of the net following a precise pass from Marlon Fossey . The visitors doubled their lead in the 24th minute when Adnane Abid clinical finish, assisted by Casper Nielsen , made it 0-2. KV Mechelen struggled to find their rhythm as the visitors dominated the opening exchanges. Mechelen’s Lifeline Before the Break Just as it looked like Lommel would head into the interval with a comfortable cushion, the hosts struck back. In the fourth minute of first-half stoppage time, Therence Koudou converted a chance created by Malcolm Lohunanu-Mbasi . The goal shifted the momentum significantly, giving the home crowd hope and providing the players with a much-needed boost heading into the locker rooms. Lommel Re-establish Control The second half saw tactical changes, including the introduction of Benito Raman for the hosts. However, Lommel United seemed to have put the game to bed in the 65th minute. Casper Nielsen provided his second assist of the match, setting up Adnane Abid for his second goal. Leading 1-3 with only 25 minutes remaining, the visitors appeared to be cruising toward a vital away victory. The Incredible Comeback The closing stages produced a sequence of events that left the stadium in awe. In the 89th minute, Myron van Brederode clinical penalty brought the score to 2-3. As tension boiled over, Lommel players Ryan Fosso and Matthieu Epolo were shown yellow cards during a frantic period of added time. In the 90+12th minute, Myron van Brederode stepped up once again to convert his second penalty of the match, completing a stunning comeback to secure a 3-3 draw in the dying embers of the game."
